    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36767" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pōcŭlentus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poscŭl-,
			pōtŭl-</span></b> ), a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>drinkable</i>, <i>potable</i>: penus est quod
			esculentum aut poculentum est, etc., Q. Scaevola ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 4, 1,
				17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of vessels, <i>fit for use in drinking</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">a poculento argento vascularius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 643, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
